From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: driver lookup ap mld name
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Recognise OpenWrt MLD netdev names (ap-mld-N) in the driver lookup.

get_wifi_driver() picks a driver by matching the interface name against the
comma-separated prefixes in wifi_driver.name. The default driver declares
"wlan,phy,bsta" and nlwifi declares "wlan". OpenWrt names the AP-MLD netdev
ap-mld-N, which matches none of them, so get_wifi_driver() returns NULL and
every libwifi call on that interface comes back -ENOTSUP.

That single miss disables the whole AP-MLD data path, silently and completely:

  wifi_get_mlo_links(ap-mld-1)         -> -ENOTSUP
  wl_apmld_status()                    -> UBUS_STATUS_UNKNOWN_ERROR
  ubus call wifi.apmld.ap-mld-1 status -> "Unknown error"
  map-agent                            -> num_ap_mld = 0
  map-agent                            -> never emits AP-MLD Config TLV (0xE0)
  map-controller                       -> apmld / affiliated_ap / ttlm stay empty

The MLD itself is up the whole time - three links, clients associated, traffic
flowing. Only the reporting path is dead, which is why it went unnoticed: the
dashboard reads the configured link list instead and shows three links either
way.

Adding the prefix is enough. The matcher takes strspn(ifname, token) and then
requires the next character to be a digit or NUL: for "ap-mld-1" and token
"ap-mld" that is s=7, ifname[7]='1', so it matches, and "ap-mld" cannot collide
with wlan/phy/bsta interfaces.

--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
@@ -2187,7 +2187,7 @@
 
 
 const struct wifi_driver default_wifi_driver = {
-	.name = "wlan,phy,bsta",
+	.name = "wlan,phy,bsta,ap-mld",
 	.info = nlwifi_driver_info,
 
 	/* Radio/phy callbacks */
